Attribution
-----------
MenuAI shows a "Powered by MenuAI · Open source" credit on every menu it renders
(editor preview, full-screen view, exported files, print), in the editor footer,
in server logs and in CLI output. Every source file carries the MenuAI license
notice. These credits are part of the project:

  * The copyright and license notices (LICENSE, this NOTICE, and the header at the
    top of each source file) must be kept in all copies, forks and substantial
    portions of the software, as required by the MIT License.
  * We ask that the visible "Powered by MenuAI" credit be kept as well. The test
    suite and CI (`npm run check:attribution`) fail if it is removed.

Third-party components keep their own licenses (fonts: SIL Open Font License 1.1,
via Fontsource; npm dependencies: see package-lock.json).
